# Requests against the running demo app.
#
#   cd app && ./mxcli run --local --ensure-db -p ViewEntityExamples.mpr
#
# App security is off in this demo, so no credentials are needed. In a real app
# the service declares `authentication basic` and every call carries
# `Authorization: Basic ...`.

@base = http://localhost:8080/odata/submissions/v1

### Service document — the four resources
GET {{base}}/

### $metadata — note contractType is Edm.String everywhere
GET {{base}}/$metadata

### Control: one row per profile per quarter, key is three Integers
GET {{base}}/QuarterSubmission?$orderby=profileNumber,quarterNo

### Control: read one row back by its key
GET {{base}}/QuarterSubmission(profileNumber=300,periodYear=2025,quarterNo=1)

### The fan-out, keyed WITHOUT the contract type — three rows share this key
GET {{base}}/QuarterSubmissionPerTypeBroken?$filter=profileNumber eq 300 and quarterNo eq 1

### ...and asking for that key returns an arbitrary one of them, with a 200
GET {{base}}/QuarterSubmissionPerTypeBroken(profileNumber=300,periodYear=2025,quarterNo=1)

### Filtering on the enumeration works — Mendix parses 'Freelance' from the query string
GET {{base}}/QuarterSubmissionPerTypeBroken?$filter=contractType eq 'Freelance'

### Workaround A: the String shadow carries the key
GET {{base}}/QuarterSubmissionPerType?$orderby=profileNumber,quarterNo,contractTypeKey

### Workaround A: read one row back by its full key
GET {{base}}/QuarterSubmissionPerType(profileNumber=300,periodYear=2025,quarterNo=1,contractTypeKey='Freelance')

### Workaround A: filter on the key attribute
GET {{base}}/QuarterSubmissionPerType?$filter=contractTypeKey eq 'Freelance'

### Workaround C: one composite id
GET {{base}}/QuarterSubmissionPerTypeById

### Workaround C: read one row back by that id
GET {{base}}/QuarterSubmissionPerTypeById('300-2025Q1-Temporary')
